# NeuraBar (Cursor rules)

The canonical, cross-tool instructions live in [AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md) — read
it first. It covers build/test, conventions, ad-hoc-signing limits, and commit
rules. This file only restates the rules Cursor most often trips on.

- **Never ship build warnings.** A clean `./build.sh` is the baseline; the
  292-test suite must stay green.
- Author commits as **Bayram Eker** `<eker600@gmail.com>` — **never** add a
  Claude / AI co-author line.
- **No in-app toasts** — user feedback flashes the menu-bar icon (~1.4s).
- Codable stores need **tolerant decoders**; never break JSON already on disk.
- macOS APIs needing a real bundle must guard with
  `Bundle.main.bundlePath.hasSuffix(".app")` (the xctest runner has no `.app`).
- Zero external dependencies — don't reach for a package; the answer is in Foundation/SwiftUI.

Architecture map: [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](mdc:docs/ARCHITECTURE.md).
Before ending a substantial session, update [docs/HANDOFF.md](mdc:docs/HANDOFF.md).
